course: dictionary
lesson: 3129
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. The word element is a good example. In «an element of surprise», element means one part or feature of something bigger.
explain: In science, an element is a pure substance made of only one kind of atom, such as oxygen, iron or gold. Each element leaves its own dark lines in starlight, «so we can tell what a star is made of».
explain: In «the kettle has a hot metal element sitting in the water», element means the metal part that gets hot, not a chemical. In «exposed to the elements», it means the weather. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you probably have it right.
explain: In maths, an element is one member of a set. «3 is an element of the set of odd numbers» means 3 is one of the odd numbers. And when you are «in your element», you are happy doing what you are good at.
fact: An element is one part or feature of something bigger, or a pure substance made of only one kind of atom.
fact: Elements such as hydrogen, helium, iron and gold are shown in the periodic table, which lists over a hundred of them.
fact: Elements combine to form compounds: water is made of hydrogen and oxygen.
fact: Long ago, people believed everything was made of four elements: earth, air, fire and water.
fact: «The elements» means the weather, especially bad weather, as in «brave the elements».
exercise: In «an element of surprise», what does element mean? | The weather | A metal part that gets hot | A pure substance found in rocks | *One part or feature of something bigger
exercise: Which of these is a chemical element? | *Oxygen | Air | Bread | Water
exercise: In «exposed to the elements», what are the elements? | Four old ideas about the world | *The weather, especially bad weather | Members of a set | Parts of a kettle
test: Kane says «3 is an element of the set of odd numbers». What does element mean in maths? | The weather | Lots of odd numbers | A metal part in a heater | *One member of a set
test: Which sentence uses element to mean the metal part that gets hot? | *«The kettle has a hot metal element» | «Braving the elements in a storm» | «She was in her element at the piano» | «Water is made of hydrogen and oxygen»
exam: In «She is in her element when she paints», what does in her element mean? | *Happy doing what she is good at | The bad weather | A metal part that gets hot | A pure substance made of one kind of atom
